Against RetroPortingToolKit/psxrecomp @ 2113defc ("Fix overlay Clang exports,
PGO, and scaffold cache", PR #344 / branch pe-feedback) -- i.e. on top of that
PR, not the pre-#344 tree. Fixes the PGO *training* step, which #344 didn't
touch: `rebuild --force-pgo` crashed with `[WinError 5] Access is denied` on
Windows, and even on a run that didn't crash, the resulting .profraw was
0 bytes. See findings/pgo-train-fix.md for the full writeup, root cause, and
verification data (real diff, tested end-to-end: 6.1MB .profraw x2, merged to
a 1MB default.profdata, full instrument->train->optimize cycle completing
with exit 0).

